  "summary": "Replaces container-specific removal idioms, such as the vector erase-remove idiom and list member removal, with C++20's std::erase and std::erase_if across 13 files. It also updates several simple iterator-based erase calls to use the standard free functions.",
  "problem": "Legacy erase patterns differ across container types: array-based containers require the two-step erase-remove idiom which is error-prone if the erase step or end iterator is mishandled, whereas node-based containers use member removal. This inconsistency leads to verbose and potentially bug-prone container mutation code.",
  "evidence": [
    "PR description notes that omitting the erase call or the end iterator in the erase-remove idiom can introduce bugs (citing clang-tidy's bugprone-inaccurate-erase and discussion in #36588)."
